## Environment

* SuperCollider version: 3.11
* Operating system: Any

## Steps to reproduce

```supercollider
Server.supernova;

// start clean
(SynthDef.synthDefDir +/+ "testMD.*").pathMatch.do(File.delete(_));

(
SynthDef(\testMD, { |out, freq = 440|
	Out.ar(out, SinOsc.ar(freq));
}).store;
)

// scsyndef file without corresponding txarcmeta file, OK
s.boot;

(
SynthDef(\testMD, { |out, freq = 440|
	Out.ar(out, SinOsc.ar(freq));
}, metadata: (specs: (freq: \freq))).store;
)

// scsyndef file WITH corresponding txarcmeta file:
s.reboot;

Exception when reading synthdef: corrupted synthdef
Exception when reading synthdef: corrupted synthdef
Exception when reading synthdef: corrupted synthdef
... over 15000 times (!)

// or, same error
s.sendMsg("/d_loadDir", SynthDef.synthDefDir);
```

## Expected vs. actual behavior

scsynth checks the file extension before trying to load a SynthDef file. If it isn't "scsyndef" then it ignores the file.

supernova appears not to include this check.

So,

Expected: Don't try to load something that you know in advance won't be in the right format.

Actual: Tries to load everything.

This is more of an issue in 3.11 because we are now writing metadata files to disk by default. Previous versions did not. (This affects *only* SynthDefs written to disk, which is already a minority of cases, and of those, only SynthDefs with contents in the metadata. But this has been reported for dkmayer's miSCellaneous library... so we have to fix it. Should be easy.)

(In some cases, supernova might crash. In the above test case, it doesn't.)

